{"id":"CVE-2008-3234","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-07-18T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T09:28:41.783Z","description":"sshd in OpenSSH 4 on Debian GNU/Linux, and the 20070303 OpenSSH snapshot, allows remote authenticated users to obtain access to arbitrary SELinux roles by appending a :/ (colon slash) sequence, followed by the role name, to the username.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/44037","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"openssh-sshd-selinuxrole-unauth-access(44037)"},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/6094","tags":["exploit","x_refsource_EXPLOIT-DB"],"name":"6094"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/30276","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"30276"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"6094","title":"Debian OpenSSH - (Authenticated) Remote SELinux Privilege Escalation","type":"remote","platform":"linux","date":"2008-07-17","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2008-3259","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-07-22T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T09:28:41.948Z","description":"OpenSSH before 5.1 sets the SO_REUSEADDR socket option when the X11UseLocalhost configuration setting is disabled, which allows local users on some platforms to hijack the X11 forwarding port via a bind to a single IP address, as demonstrated on the HP-UX platform.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/2148","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2008-2148"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/30339","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"30339"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/43940","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"openssh-x11forwarding-info-disclosure(43940)"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/31179","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"31179"},{"url":"http://openssh.com/security.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1020537","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1020537"},{"url":"http://www.openssh.com/txt/release-5.1","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2008-3844","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-08-27T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T09:53:00.389Z","description":"Certain Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 4 and 5 packages for OpenSSH, as signed in August 2008 using a legitimate Red Hat GPG key, contain an externally introduced modification (Trojan Horse) that allows the package authors to have an unknown impact.  NOTE: since the malicious packages were not distributed from any official Red Hat sources, the scope of this issue is restricted to users who may have obtained these packages through unofficial distribution points.  As of 20080827, no unofficial distributions of this software are known.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://support.avaya.com/elmodocs2/security/ASA-2008-399.htm","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/security/data/openssh-blacklist.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/2821","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2008-2821"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/31575","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"31575"},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2008-0855.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2008:0855"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/44747","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"openssh-rhel-backdoor(44747)"},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1020730","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1020730"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/30794","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"30794"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/32241","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"32241"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2008-4109","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-09-17T18:06:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T10:00:42.727Z","description":"A certain Debian patch for OpenSSH before 4.3p2-9etch3 on etch; before 4.6p1-1 on sid and lenny; and on other distributions such as SUSE uses functions that are not async-signal-safe in the signal handler for login timeouts, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (connection slot exhaustion) via multiple login attempts. NOTE: this issue exists because of an incorrect fix for CVE-2006-5051.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/usn-649-1","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"USN-649-1"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/45202","tags":["vdb-entry"],"name":"openssh-signalhandler-dos(45202)"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/31885","tags":["third-party-advisory"],"name":"31885"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1020891","tags":["vdb-entry"],"name":"1020891"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2008/dsa-1638","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-1638"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2008-10/msg00004.html","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"SUSE-SR:2008:020"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/32080","tags":["third-party-advisory"],"name":"32080"},{"url":"http://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=498678"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/32181","tags":["third-party-advisory"],"name":"32181"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/07/01/3","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[oss-security] 20240701 CVE-2024-6387: RCE in OpenSSH's server, on glibc-based Linux systems"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2008-5161","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-11-19T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-05-28T18:11:36.859Z","description":"Error handling in the SSH protocol in (1) SSH Tectia Client and Server and Connector 4.0 through 4.4.11, 5.0 through 5.2.4, and 5.3 through 5.3.8; Client and Server and ConnectSecure 6.0 through 6.0.4; Server for Linux on IBM System z 6.0.4; Server for IBM z/OS 5.5.1 and earlier, 6.0.0, and 6.0.1; and Client 4.0-J through 4.3.3-J and 4.0-K through 4.3.10-K; and (2) OpenSSH 4.7p1 and possibly other versions, when using a block cipher algorithm in Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) mode, makes it easier for remote attackers to recover certain plaintext data from an arbitrary block of ciphertext in an SSH session via unknown vectors.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-329 CWE-329 Generation of Predictable IV with CBC Mode"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":3.7,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://openssh.org/txt/cbc.adv","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://sunsolve.sun.com/search/document.do?assetkey=1-66-247186-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUNALERT"],"name":"247186"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/32319","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"32319"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/33121","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"33121"},{"url":"https://h20566.www2.hpe.com/portal/site/hpsc/public/kb/docDisplay?docId=emr_na-c05157667","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://osvdb.org/49872","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"49872"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/33308","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"33308"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2009-1287.html","tags":["